    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0769" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg760"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/4913: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-09T12:00:00-06:00">October 9,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>400. Referring to my telegram number 397 of October 6, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d709-f1"/> Supreme Court decided on October 8<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d709-f2"/> not to take action on question <pb facs="0770" n="761"
                        xml:id="pg761"/> of constitutionality of decree of March 18 and
                    expropriation law of 1936. Basis of decision was that executive power had not as
                    yet resolved the appeal entered with administrative authorities by the companies
                    against the expropriation action. See third paragraph my telegram number 390 of
                    September 29, 1938.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d709-f3"/> Air mail despatch
                    follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
